{"book":24,"chapter":24,"context":{"chapter":24,"title":"Two Baskets of Figs","summary":"After King Jeconiah and Judah's leaders and craftsmen are taken to Babylon, Jeremiah sees two baskets of figs at the temple, one very good and one rotten. The good figs are the exiles, whom God will bring back with a heart to know Him; the bad figs are Zedekiah and those who stayed or fled to Egypt.","background":"The vision follows the deportation of 597 BC (2 Kings 24:10-16). Those left in Jerusalem tended to think they were God's favored ones and the exiles were cursed. God's verdict is the reverse: His future lies with the people in Babylon.","customs":[{"term":"Figs that are first ripe","verses":"24:2","note":"Early figs ripened in early summer before the main crop and were a prized delicacy (compare Hosea 9:10)."}],"watchFor":["'Build them, and not pull them down… plant them, and not pluck them up' (v. 6) echoes 1:10.","'An heart to know me' (v. 7) anticipates the new covenant of 31:33."],"connections":["2 Kings 24:10-16","Jeremiah 29:16-19","Ezekiel 11:15-20","Hosea 9:10"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["הִרְאַנִי","hir'ani","H7200","HVhp3ms/Sp1bs","he showed me"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["וְהִנֵּה","vehineh","H2009","HC/Tj","and there!"],["שְׁנֵי","shenei","H8147","HAcbdc","two"],["דּוּדָאֵי","duda'ei","H1731","HNcmpc","baskets of"],["תְאֵנִים","te'enim","H8384","HNcmpa","figs"],["מוּעָדִים","mu'adim","H3259","HVHsmpa","[were] set"],["לִפְנֵי","lifnei","H6440","HR/Ncmpc","<to> before"],["הֵיכַל","heikhal","H1964","HNcmsc","[the] temple of"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["אַחֲרֵי","'acharei","H310","HAcmpc","after"],["הַגְלוֹת","haglot","H1540","HVhcc","took into exile"],["נְבוּכַדְרֶאצַּר","nevukhadretzar","H5019","HNpm","Nebuchadnezzar"],["מֶלֶךְ","melekh-","H4428","HNcmsc","[the] king of"],["בָּבֶל","bavel","H894","HNpl","Babylon"],["אֶת","'et-","H853","HTo","<obj.>"],["יְכָנְיָהוּ","yekhaneyahu","H3204","HNpm","Jeconiah"],["בֶן","ven-","H1121